  "body": "Per https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1360190#c9 there is some concern with enabling SharedArrayBuffer to be used with MessageChannel.\r\n\r\nIn effect, the standard requires a design where a posted SharedArrayBuffer is kept on the sending side until the receiver claims it. If at the time the receiver claims it it's in a different process, this'll fail. If it's in the same process, it'll get a handle to the underlying data.\r\n\r\nThis doesn't seem too bad to me, but reportedly Google is not having it and @lars-t-hansen doesn't seem enthused either.\r\n\r\n(Note that if we were to accept this as a problem, this effectively means that this implementation decision forces a redesign of the standard, which has used MessageChannel as the underlying mechanism to communicate with a dedicated worker.)",
